  "title": "legacy, redis, aside, relaxed",
  "summary": "A shared Redis with a recorded maxmemory and allkeys-lru policy (approximate LRU, and the report says so). Cache-aside: a miss takes a per-key fill lease, double-checks, loads a committed view and publishes it. A reader may receive an older committed value than the latest acknowledged write, and every such read is counted. The legacy model supplies no token, so strict freshness rests on invalidation alone or on an authoritative read.",
  "risk": "may return stale committed data; throughput is only reportable with the wrong-read count and rate beside it",
